                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How'd this pass without an SOB?  We you able to upload it because you're a Gerrit admin?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Not sure why it let me (I've seen that message before).  It's been fixed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/gb200nvl-obmc.cfg",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@andrew@codeconstruct.com.au - I don't recognize \"FLOWS\".  Do we want that everywhere?\n\nI don't know how we decide which TRANSPORTs we should enable... do we want to just enable them all from the `df-mctp`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/gb200nvl-obmc.cfg",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/gb200nvl-obmc.cfg",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "MCTP_FLOWS is meant to handle scenarios where a single request message an generate multiple response messages (ex: NVMe-MI). It is useful in muxed I2C topologies to make sure that the mux stays locked on a given target, until the userspace app releases the flow"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/gb200nvl-obmc.cfg",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "`CONFIG_MCTP_FLOWS` is automatically selected when relevant transports (such as `CONFIG_MCTP_TRANSPORT_I2C`) are selected:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/linux/blob/dev-6.6/drivers/net/mctp/Kconfig#L30\n\nAlso, `CONFIG_MCTP_TRANSPORT_I3C` should go in `meta-phosphor/recipes-kernel/linux/mctp/mctp.cfg`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/gb200nvl-obmc.cfg",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/79808 meta-phosphor\n\nAdded i3c above.\n\nThis patchset has been updated to remove i3c."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-phosphor/pldm/files/host_eid",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Interesting that we need this... I wonder what's going on with PLDM by default.  I see a `oem-ibm` config setting that installs one with `18` but we don't enable that on meta-facebook.\n\n@manojkiran.eda@gmail.com - Is this something we should fix in PLDM?  I see some layers setting it to 0 and some setting it to 18."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-phosphor/pldm/files/host_eid",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks like the code default initializes the eid to zero (using {}, so doesn't seem intentional) then doesn't handle errors on reading in the file\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/4bf3ed840f13c31720ffa7c255942f3836402f4f/common/utils.cpp#L139\n\nHard to tell if the \"eid zero is the default\" behavior is on purpose from that chunk of code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nvidia/meta-gb200nvl-obmc/recipes-phosphor/pldm/files/host_eid",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed this change for now."
                }
            ],
